          "date": "2026-11-09 10:46:05.000000000",
          "tz": 0
        },
        "subject": "LU-18133 tests: check setstripe in sanity 398m",
        "message": "LU-18133 tests: check setstripe in sanity 398m\n\nsanity 398m ignores the result of \"lfs setstripe -o 0,1,0,1\".\nWhen it fails (ENOSPC is seen in CI, as the MDS can still see an OST\nas full after a preceding test), the file gets default striping, the\ninjected bulk write failure never hits the first stripe and the test\nreports that the dio write succeeded.\n\nWait for deletes and MDS/OST sync first, retry setstripe for up to\n30 seconds, and fail with a clear error if it never works.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial testlist=sanity env=ONLY=\"398l 398m\"\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-sonnet-5-5\nSigned-off-by: Patrick Farrell <patrick@thelustrecollective.com>\nChange-Id: If1969dd8097a9edf9137bfe95a80064dea1c87ce\n"
      },
